    "crossref": {
      "source": "crossref",
      "found": true,
      "raw": {},
      "title": "10 years of ISA: lessons learned and recent development",
      "abstract": "<ns3:p>A quick tour of the experience garnered over the years developing and using the ISA model and tools to manage multi-omics data.</ns3:p>\n                <ns3:p>The presentation highlights the capability of the Investigation Study Assay model to represent experimental metadata, its extensibility allowing it to support transcriptomics, metabolomics, and other molecular phenotyping methods.</ns3:p>\n                <ns3:p>The presentation highlights how various communities have adopted the format and how tool developers have built applications and extension.</ns3:p>\n                <ns3:p>Finally, the presentation covers recent development, including the ISA GraphQL and ISA RDF linked data generation, which support a variety of context options (wikidata, obofoundry or schema.org).</ns3:p>",
